--- 3. re-calibrate on all days so far
# Calibration report (2026-09-25)

1940 rows, 357 tokens, 3 day(s) (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-25). Target: cost of selling immediately across all measured venues, vs consolidated mid. 5-fold CV grouped by token.
1625 more sales could not be absorbed by the merged book at all (no venue truncated). They can't be fitted, so they're scored instead: 'false comfort' = share a model prices under 10%. Dropped: 338 sales where a venue capped its levels (thin vs truncated unknowable); 0 token-days with no CMC volume/sigma.

| model | Y | delta | median abs err | median factor off | R^2 (log) | false comfort |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| textbook sqrt, global Y **(shipped)** | 1.94 | 0.500 | 15.4 bps | x1.81 | 0.468 | 79% |
| power law, global Y | 8.88 | 0.727 | 16.6 bps | x1.77 | 0.510 | 43% |
| learned Y per token | per token | 0.727 | 15.4 bps | x1.72 | 0.570 | 44% |

Median absolute error by order size (out-of-fold, bps):

| size | n | sqrt | power | learned |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| $10,000 | 866 | 9.0 | 8.1 | 7.4 |
| $100,000 | 773 | 25.4 | 34.7 | 31.8 |
| $1,000,000 | 242 | 25.5 | 35.6 | 39.1 |
| $10,000,000 | 59 | 82.1 | 66.9 | 94.7 |

What predicts a token's Y (GBM feature importance): log_sigma 0.49, history_days 0.15, turnover 0.15, log_mcap 0.11, log_volume 0.11

The learned model did not beat the power law by the required 5%, so the power law ships. Published as a negative result.

Wrote ingest/calibration.json (used by impact.py) and data/calibration_report.md (for METHODOLOGY.md).
